# A dive into the Mandelbrot set and back out, with its colors cycling.
#
# The whole of the module in three wires: a slow triangle on 'zoom' is the dive, the
# clock on 'shift' turns the colors, and 'color' goes straight to the screen. The
# middle is Seahorse Valley, the crease between the main body and the bulb to its
# left, where the detail never runs out. Down to ten halvings and back up in a
# minute, starting at the top: a steady ramp on zoom is a steady dive.

description "A dive into the Mandelbrot set and back out, its colors cycling as it"
  "goes."
tags "patterns"

requires flyback.fractals

triangle(freq: 0.016666668, phase: 0.5, amp: 5, bias: 5)
  |> mandelbrot(
      re: -0.7436439,
      im: 0.1318259,
      zoom: _,
      shift: t * 0.04,
      iterations: "128")
  |> out.color
out.volume = 0
